                <pb facs="0693" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.825/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-25T17:00:00-04:00">June 25, 1934—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>185. Your 258, June 21, 11 a.m. and 260, June 21, 4 p.m. in regard to pilotage.
                    The Legation’s action, taken in conjunction with the interested heads of
                    Legation (other than the German Minister), in acquiescing in the precautionary
                    plan suggested by the Shanghai Consular Body has the Department’s approval.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
